components-counter-counterbutton.description:
button_counter (Figma 502:9109): a 44 × 44 hit area with a 36 px white circle.

Press feedback follows the fluid-interface rules:
- it starts on pointer-down, not on release (the circle shrinks 36 → 32 in 100 ms, ease-out);
- release is slower (240 ms) so the circle settles back instead of snapping;
- it is a CSS transition, so a quick tap reverses mid-way from wherever the circle is;
- sliding the finger off cancels the press, like a native button.
The value changes on click (pointer-up), the way native steppers commit.

